; Stage 15 B4 (name-resolution.md §8.2's per-kind rule, §14.2's `collides`
; column). An enum registers its MEMBERS in `g-globals` but never its own name,
; so `BK-ENUM` carried `collides` 0 and nothing in the one-symbol-one-kind walk
; ever probed `g-enumdefs`. This file compiled clean before B4, with `Colour`
; naming both a type usable in an annotation and a function.
;
; The blame lands on the `defn`, not the `defenum`: `guard-name-kind` reports at
; whichever definer is emitted second (conventions.md, "One name-kind priority
; order").

(defenum Colour Colour-Red Colour-Green)

(defn Colour ():i32 (return 1))

(defn main ():i32 (return (Colour)))
